changed_sources=[n for n,v in hashes.items() if hashlib.sha256((H/n).read_bytes()).hexdigest()!=v]
text='''CENTRABUS continuous V5 evidence development — 2026-10-20

The separate development runtime is `/home/centrabus/camera_calibration/centrabus_fast_runtime_v5_evidence_dev_20261020`. The original continuous runtime is unchanged (all starting source/document hashes rechecked). No physical camera was opened during this work. No Supabase integration or verified numerical calibration was added.

**FUEL evidence and the limit on the original rejection diagnosis.** The actual annotated Cycles 7 and 8 from `session_20261020_010623_790726_3565_de3491ea` were inspected at full size and in enlarged crops. Both visibly contain a long upper-left shaft leading toward the physical hub, with a red warning block beside the blade. The other five original overlays visually agree with their shafts. Their early-session OIL angles are about 108 degrees, with existing UNVERIFIED mapped values around 28%.

The live `ambiguous_shaft_or_endpoint` label is generated when `fuel_geometry.status` is not verified or its recorded angle/base/tip do not match the returned candidate. The underlying audit tests proximal fit spread, whole/proximal disagreement, hub residual, radial occupancy, distal branching, endpoint deviation, endpoint pixels and endpoint stability. The saved label does not identify which sub-check failed. Raw in-memory frames and audit metrics from those cycles were not saved. Re-decoding the actual annotated JPEGs with the old local detector passes the audit. Consequently the precise original failing sub-check cannot be established, and this report does not claim that its threshold was proven wrong or that the new code has been tested on those absent raw pixels.

What the available pixels do establish: strict HSV segmentation clips the distal blade in both JPEGs. The strict selected shaft contains 1,285/1,438 pixels; separate warning components contain 422/511 pixels. The relaxed mask reconnects the missing tip but joins the warning block, producing 2,880/2,976-pixel components. Whole relaxed fits are 147.716/147.362 degrees and include the marking. Proximal shaft fits instead agree near 134 degrees. Simply accepting the relaxed whole component would be incorrect. In the distal completion regions, 153/187 and 164/178 selected pixels fail the strict hue ranges; median OpenCV hue is 163 in both, below the high-red cutoff of 165. Only 32/187 and 10/178 pixels meet all strict HSV thresholds before morphology. Some additional pixels fail saturation too. The relaxed high-red range starts at 160. This directly explains clipping on the available decoded JPEGs; the missing original raw hue/mask is not reconstructible. [Distal colour evidence](review/session/distal_colour_evidence.json).

The measured geometry below is from the decoded saved JPEG with re-estimated registration; it is not a reconstruction of original raw-camera metadata. The known 74-pixel header and 170-pixel footer are removed for coordinate work. FUEL has no burned-in needle overlay in these two images. Other gauges do, so these images are not valid raw full-dashboard regression fixtures. Registration and mask membership can differ after drawn overlays and JPEG re-encoding, although detector thresholds are unchanged.

| Cycle | JPEG strict fit → completed shaft | Base, local pixels | Tip, local pixels | Span, pixels | Registered local hub / scale |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
'''
for r in rows:
 a,b=r['before'],r['after'];n=int(r['file'].split('_')[1]);text+=f"| {n} | {a['angle']:.3f}° → {b['angle']:.3f}° | {a['base']} → {b['base']} | {a['tip']} → {b['tip']} | {a['line_span']:.2f} → {b['line_span']:.2f} | ({r['hub'][0]:.2f}, {r['hub'][1]:.2f}) / {r['scale']:.4f} |\n"
text+='''
Cycle 7/8 proximal angle spreads are 0.389/1.353 degrees; distal endpoint spreads are 0.663/2.237 pixels. Proposed tips are 0.804/0.043 pixels from supporting selected mask pixels. Both shafts have full radial occupancy with no empty continuity bins, and all strict selected pixels agree with the recovered shaft corridor. The warning block is excluded from the completed mask and the centre line follows the visible blade. Pixel precision does not imply sub-degree physical calibration accuracy.

[Original full Cycle 7](../centrabus_fast_runtime_v5_continuous_dev_20261020/annotations/session_20261020_010623_790726_3565_de3491ea/cycle_007_20261020_010637_292169_annotated.jpg), [original full Cycle 8](../centrabus_fast_runtime_v5_continuous_dev_20261020/annotations/session_20261020_010623_790726_3565_de3491ea/cycle_008_20261020_010638_737903_annotated.jpg).

[Cycle 7 actual saved before / offline recovered after](review/session/010623_cycle_007_actual_before_offline_after.jpg), [Cycle 8 comparison](review/session/010623_cycle_008_actual_before_offline_after.jpg). The retained FUEL UNCERTAIN text inside each source crop belongs to the original saved image; the separate after caption identifies the offline overlay. [Cycle 7 masks](review/session/010623_cycle_007_mask_evidence.jpg), [Cycle 8 masks](review/session/010623_cycle_008_mask_evidence.jpg), [full measurements](review/session/measurements.json), [first ten original annotations contact sheet](review/session/actual_ten_contact.jpg).

**Implemented correction.** `fuel_shaft.py` adds strict-shaft completion; `fuel_angle_refinement.py` invokes it after the original audit when no existing branch correction was returned. It applies only to a strict candidate with at least 50 scaled pixels of support. A single relaxed connected component must contain at least 90% of the strict pixels. The existing branch-separation audit must independently return a verified replacement, retaining its <=3-degree proximal spread, <=20-scaled-pixel hub residual, <=12-scaled-pixel proximal p90, >=70-scaled-pixel shaft, >=90% continuity, <=1 gap bin, <=10-scaled-pixel endpoint spread and <=3-scaled-pixel tip support gates.

Additional agreement requires >=85% of strict pixels in the recovered corridor, >=50 scaled pixels of strict longitudinal span, <=5-degree strict/recovered direction disagreement, 12–40 scaled pixels of tip extension, <=12 scaled pixels of base movement and a proximal endpoint within 85 scaled pixels of the registered hub. Already separated warning-mark corrections are retained. No path directly accepts an unaudited relaxed fit, disables ambiguity, hard-codes a frame/name/angle, uses a prior result, or captures another image. A tested colour perturbation still remains ambiguous. This addresses observed clipping and improves supported endpoint evidence; raw Cycle 7/8 rejection recovery remains to be checked in a new physical session.

**Later-cycle investigation.** There is no saved image or camera metadata for Cycle 25 onward. No registration, focus, exposure or component-selection cause is proven for that interval. The early ten images show roughly vertical FRONT/REAR blades and a more upright OIL blade; they cannot establish the later state.

The registration direction is correct: ORB fits current→reference and the inverse maps reference ROI centres/hubs to current pixels. No perspective-warped image is passed to a gauge: each reader receives original-pixel axis-aligned crops. Projective selection requires spatially distributed inliers, residual/scale/anisotropy/orientation checks and a spatial jackknife. The known-transform tests pass. Per-frame ORB/RANSAC selection can nevertheless switch models or fail under changing features; only reference descriptors are cached, with no temporal stabilization. Same-frame projective fallback is already present and remains unchanged. Historical raw saved examples demonstrate genuine registration sensitivity: manifest IDs 261/263/264 have only 15/16/14 similarity inliers, with the projective fit rejected for four occupied cells; nearby 262/265 use supported projective fits. These examples support a possible mechanism, not attribution to continuous Cycle 25. The original safety gates suppress globally unsupported alignment.

Continuous AF, AE and AWB remain enabled, so focus hunting or colour/exposure changes are possible. No historical LensPosition/AfState/ExposureTime/gain series was saved, so there is no measured focus/exposure change to correlate with the later failures. JPEG sharpness of a frame containing drawn overlays is not a trustworthy replacement for that missing raw evidence. The installed Picamera2 `make_array` copies camera-buffer pixels, and the request is released after copying; inspection does not support recycled buffer memory as the explanation.

FRONT/REAR can become uncertain when only short radial fragments survive or a merged scale fails independent connected-shaft evidence. BATTERY can fail registered/local hub and shaft checks. These existing guards and per-gauge exception boundaries are retained, rather than relaxed without late-frame evidence.

**OIL=0.0%.** `_angle_to_percent` clamps every angle >=135 degrees to 0%. The baseline OIL reader selects a red connected component within a pivot-centred radial band by area/axis-aligned elongation. It does not give every long strict candidate an independent proximal shaft/endpoint audit; the V5 relaxed replacement is sought only for a short original span. Wrong registration, warning/scale contamination or changed colour support can therefore produce a plausible but incorrect candidate. No such error is established for the unrecorded later cycles. Six inspected historical raw examples have physical blades pointing farther left and measured angles 136.38–141.53 degrees, consistent with that image direction and the existing zero clamp ([historical OIL figure](review/historical_oil_zero.jpg)). Some overlays are shortened. Those historical directions do not verify a numerical zero or the later continuous reading. A numeric OIL field means that the existing gates passed for that cycle; physical correctness still requires the corresponding image. OIL calibration, mapping and detection code were not changed without corresponding evidence.

**Regression and review.** The full 293 saved raw/prerecorded-frame manifest was rerun with the new detector. It includes every previous FUEL warning-mark case, the prior BATTERY/FRONT failure captures, and all 37 saved captures in the latest 13-cycle dataset. Historical attempts are independent fixtures, never automatic capture retries.

| Dataset | Frames | Candidates / possible | DETECTED | UNCERTAIN | UNDETECTED |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
'''
